 "about": "Closed clockwise pentagon (stroke 6, miter join) against InDesign 2025: path alignment Top/Bottom (typepath-c10). Start 0 on the closing vertex of a non-rectangle is a numeric tie in InDesign (start 0 or the offset length), so those ranges are not in the set; ranges that end within a trimmed inner corner come out as a tiny difference of two float32 sums (0.8285 past the offset length), too small for the oracle's 1e-6 tolerance, and stay out too (unit test in model/src/textpath.rs). Pentagon spacing -6 (inward offset on a polygon) stays out: print change error 1.13, the cause is not found (a rectangle's -6 and -12 pass, 0.12)."
